Day 3 Notes – Responsive CSS:
1. Media Queries
Used to make the website look good on different screen sizes.

@media (max-width: 768px) {
  /* CSS for mobile */
}

-max-width: 768px → Applies styles when screen is 768px or smaller
-Most common breakpoint for mobile

2. Changing Flex Direction:

header {
  flex-direction: column;
}

-On mobile, header items stack vertically instead of staying in a row.

3. Transition (Smooth Effect):
transition: color 0.3s ease;

-Makes hover effects smooth instead of sudden
-0.3s = time
-ease = speed style

4. Important Responsive Ideas
-Always test with browser DevTools (mobile view)
-Use flex-direction: column for mobile layouts
-Reduce padding/margin on small screens
-Keep text readable

5. Best Practice
-Write desktop CSS first → then add media queries for mobile.

